1,Torricelli languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torricelli_languages,"The Torricelli languages are unusual among Papuan languages in having a basic clause order of SVO (subject-verb-object); in contrast, most Papuan languages have SOV order. It was previously believed that the Torricelli word order was a result of contact with Austronesian languages, but Donohue (2005) believes it is more likely that SVO order was present in the Torricelli proto-language. [4 ...",Laeko-Libuat,Torricelli
